kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui60,"markdown-render-component","The TUI MUST provide a MarkdownRenderer component (src/app/tui/components/markdown.rs) that consumes a finalized string plus a MarkdownStyle and produces Vec<Line> for the ratatui buffer; RenderedLine::UserInput and RenderedLine::AssistantText MUST both render through this shared MarkdownRenderer, differing only in the injected MarkdownStyle (user_prompt palette vs assistant palette), so user input and LLM replies share identical structural rendering. The renderer MUST be backed by pulldown-cmark (not a hand-written parser). Evidence: codex uses pulldown-cmark + syntect (markdown_render.rs:825-863); pi uses marked.lexer + MarkdownTheme function injection with user/assistant sharing one Markdown class (assistant-message.ts:103 vs user-message.ts:31); kimi-code reuses pi-tui Markdown.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui61,"markdown-scope-mvp","The MarkdownRenderer MVP MUST render at minimum: headings (#), bold/code inline, fenced code blocks (with language label and background color, but WITHOUT syntect syntax highlighting), unordered lists, blockquotes, and CJK-aware paragraph wrapping (reusing existing unicode-width). The MVP MUST NOT include: syntect syntax highlighting, table rendering, OSC8 hyperlinks, or streaming incremental markdown parsing. Streaming text in the mutable last line stays plain text; markdown rendering applies only after a line is finalized and committed to scrollback. Evidence: pi table rendering alone is 170+ lines (renderTable 685-857); codex streaming uses plain-text-then-replace (AgentMarkdownCell consolidates after stream end); both confirm streaming incremental parsing is not worth MVP complexity.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui60,"user-assistant-shared-renderer",the TUI rendering source is inspected,"RenderedLine::UserInput and AssistantText rendering paths are checked","both call MarkdownRenderer with different MarkdownStyle (user_prompt vs assistant palette), not two separate rendering implementations"
  tui60,"code-block-structured",an assistant reply containing a fenced code block with language tag,the reply is finalized and committed to scrollback,"the code block renders with a language label and distinct background color (structure visible), even though syntax highlighting is not applied"
  tui61,"no-syntect-in-mvp",Cargo.toml and the markdown component source are inspected,dependencies are checked,"pulldown-cmark is present and syntect is absent (MVP does only structural code block rendering)"
  tui61,"streaming-stays-plain",streaming text is arriving in the mutable last line,"the tail frame is rendered mid-stream",the mutable line shows plain text (no markdown parsing); markdown rendering is applied only after the line is finalized
